  "slug": "eastern-mediterranean-university",
  "name": "Eastern Mediterranean University",
  "country": "Northern Cyprus",
  "city": "Famagusta",
  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Eastern Mediterranean University (EMU / Doğu Akdeniz Üniversitesi) is a state university established in 1979, located in Famagusta, Northern Cyprus. The campus is situated in the heart of the city and serves over 16,000 students from more than 110 countries, with approximately 1,100 academics from 35 countries. EMU offers instruction primarily in English and Turkish, supported by an English Preparatory School. The university holds memberships in the International Association of Universities, European University Association, Community of Mediterranean Universities, and Federation of the Universities of the Islamic World, and is one of five universities in the region accredited by ABET in engineering. EMU appeared in the 601–800 band of the Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026."
    ]
  },
